diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 7d51dc4..199fbf0 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -55,3 +55,65 @@ bin/rails test test/controllers/bots_controller_test.rb \
   test/controllers/bots/messages_controller_test.rb test/models/user/bot_test.rb
 bin/rails test test/system/bots_test.rb
 ```
+
+## Mention webhooks
+
+Set **Webhook URL** on either bot form to receive mention callbacks. It is
+optional; saving an empty field removes it. The URL must be HTTP(S), with no
+embedded username/password or fragment. HTTPS is recommended.
+
+Bots appear in the same mention autocomplete as people in rooms they belong to.
+A newly created human-authored message queues one `Message::BotWebhookJob` for
+each distinct active, mentioned member bot with a webhook. Neither DNS nor HTTP
+runs in the message-posting request. Production uses the existing Resque workers;
+development uses Rails' asynchronous adapter. Edits and bot-authored messages do
+not trigger callbacks (the latter prevents bot reply loops).
+
+Each callback is an HTTP POST with `Content-Type: application/json`:
+
+```json
+{
+  "event": "mention",
+  "author": { "id": 7, "name": "Alice" },
+  "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/BOT_CODE/messages" },
+  "message": {
+    "id": 118,
+    "body": {
+      "text": "restart the build please",
+      "html": "<div class=\"trix-content\">… full rich-text body …</div>"
+    },
+    "link": "/rooms/5/@118"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Only the addressed bot's mention attachments are removed from `body.text`;
+other mentions and ordinary text remain. `body.html` retains the full rendered
+rich text. Paths are relative to the Campfire origin. **Treat `room.reply_to` as a
+secret:** it contains this bot's posting credential. It can be used later with
+the raw-text posting API described above.
+
+To reply immediately, return `200` with `Content-Type: text/plain` or `text/html`
+(optional charset parameters are supported) and a UTF-8 response body. Plain
+text is escaped with line breaks preserved; HTML goes through the normal Action
+Text rendering/sanitization. The reply is created and broadcast as the bot and
+uses the usual room notifications. Return `204` for no reply. Other statuses,
+unsupported content types, empty bodies, invalid UTF-8, and oversized replies
+are ignored.
+
+Delivery uses the existing public-address restriction, pins the resolved IP,
+and does not use proxies or follow redirects. Local/private network endpoints
+are blocked; use a publicly reachable endpoint when developing integrations.
+Connection timeout is 5 seconds, read/write timeouts are 10 seconds, and replies
+are limited to 1 MiB. Failures do not affect the human's message and are not
+automatically retried. Membership, active status, and webhook presence are
+checked at execution time and again before posting a response. Deleted source
+records are discarded by the job.
+
+Additional regression checks:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails test test/models/message/bot_webhook_test.rb \
+  test/jobs/message/bot_webhook_job_test.rb \
+  test/controllers/autocompletable/users_controller_test.rb
+```
